# Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. .env.local is git-ignored: never commit it.
# On Vercel the same names go in Settings > Environment Variables (Production).
# Step-by-step guide: docs/setup.md, or the /setup page of the running app.

# --- Required: your Google Sheet -------------------------------------------------------------
# The spreadsheet's ID: the part of its address between /d/ and /edit.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID=
# The service account's JSON key. On your computer, point at the file (it lives in ./secrets, which is git-ignored).
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_FILE=./secrets/service-account.json
# On a host there is no file: paste the whole JSON (or base64 of it) here instead. It wins over the file when both are set.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=

# --- Required on a host: sign-in with Google -------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to run on your own computer: with ALLOWED_EMAIL unset, `npm run dev` doesn't ask you to sign in.
# A production build refuses to serve anything until all four are set.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The one Google address that may sign in (one address, not a list).
# ALLOWED_EMAIL=
# 32+ random characters: openssl rand -base64 48
# SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Optional: your name and time zone -------------------------------------------------------
# The name in "Good afternoon, <name>". Without it the greeting has no name.
# OWNER_NAME=
# An IANA zone such as America/New_York. India's (Asia/Kolkata) if unset. Baked into the build: redeploy after changing it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TIME_ZONE=

# --- Optional: import statements from Gmail (read-only) --------------------------------------
# All five or none. Get the refresh token once with `npm run authorize-gmail`.
# GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GMAIL_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# The Gmail labels your statement emails are filed under, exactly as written in Gmail.
# GMAIL_STATEMENT_LABEL=
# GMAIL_ACCOUNT_STATEMENT_LABEL=

# --- Optional: connect Claude to your app ----------------------------------------------------
# 32+ random characters. Without it /api/mcp is off.
# MCP_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# --- Optional: the daily statement sync on Vercel --------------------------------------------
# 32+ random characters. Without it the cron route is off. Leave it unset if you don't use the Gmail import.
# CRON_SECRET=
